.TH VAULT-INIT 1 "September 2026" "vault" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vault-init \- create an empty vault
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vault init
.RB [ \-\-vault
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-filler
.IR SIZE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates the vault directory, with \fBrecords/\fR and \fBobjects/\fR each
sharded into 256 subdirectories. It writes at least \fISIZE\fR bytes of
unreadable filler so that real files cannot be told apart from it by anyone
lacking the right passphrase. Filler is always written, even when \fISIZE\fR is 0.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-vault " DIR"
Vault directory. Default: $VAULT_DIR, else ~/.vault/store.
.TP
.BI \-\-filler " SIZE"
Minimum filler, in bytes, with an optional K, M, G or T suffix (powers of
1024), e.g. 500M or 2G. Default: 0.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vault (1),
.BR vault\-genkey (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Andy Dixon <vault@dixon.cx>, https://www.dixon.cx
